{"title":"2005 CEMC Gauss (Grade 7) Problems/Problem 8","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_7)_Problems/Problem_8&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>In the diagram, what is the measure of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/7/2/0728bebb477a2636300c56851b6a6f9e382c1b83.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle ACB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"57\" height=\"14\" /> in degrees?\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/4/3/8433688be652947a200ff890c99648e6c1e3d361.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] size(300); draw((-60,0)--(0,0)); draw((0,0)--(64.3,76.6)--(166,0)--cycle); label(&quot;$A$&quot;,(64.3,76.6),N); label(&quot;$93^\\circ$&quot;,(64.3,73),S); label(&quot;$130^\\circ$&quot;,(0,0),NW); label(&quot;$B$&quot;,(0,0),S); label(&quot;$D$&quot;,(-60,0),S); label(&quot;$C$&quot;,(166,0),S); [/asy]\" width=\"502\" height=\"208\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/8/5/6857b28a8c9b79d8d4370979a05c13147b10e799.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\text{(A)}\\ 57^\\circ \\qquad \\text{(B)}\\ 37^\\circ \\qquad \\text{(C)}\\ 47^\\circ \\qquad \\text{(D)}\\ 60^\\circ \\qquad \\text{(E)}\\ 17^\\circ$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"412\" height=\"17\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_7)_Problems/Problem_8&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/2/4/524569e17ffd4b6cbda1a204e4d51a32d153a70a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle ABC + \\angle ABD = 180^\\circ$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"191\" height=\"14\" /> (in other words, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/3/a/a3ad57710b6810476e6017ea2c2cc6d41219c218.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"57\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/3/f93e72b9d2c86f197276a931aba77c472d0511c6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle ABD$\" width=\"56\" height=\"13\" /> are supplementary) and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/5/6/15650219e3eef3a80eaf9c488702e13c8dd896cf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle ABD = 130^\\circ$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"114\" height=\"13\" />, then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/5/dc5a27130f375ffba6f8d69e0de0334293d0464b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle ABC = 50^\\circ$\" width=\"103\" height=\"13\" />.  Since the sum of the angles in triangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/a/e2a559986ed5a0ffc5654bd367c29dfc92913c36.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"44\" height=\"14\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/4/4/c4460b5100c3ce982ab5ebb20a8c3871e9cfdc54.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$180^\\circ$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"33\" height=\"13\" /> and we know two angles <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/9/7/1979f25404ed601750a1c6c389b2a2284ae11e6d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$93^\\circ$\" width=\"24\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/6/8/46853828ad371bf8327abee8d74f620270c06b75.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$50^\\circ$\" width=\"24\" height=\"13\" /> which add to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/e/8/2e8901249f07af27387a52a9751f49bcafd38a95.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$143^\\circ$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"33\" height=\"13\" />, then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/5/3/e535a0375f38a7ed3c60c08ee22010a32f19693b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle ACB = 180^\\circ - 143^\\circ = 37^\\circ$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"220\" height=\"13\" />.  The answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_7)_Problems/Problem_8&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_7)\" title=\"2005 CEMC Gauss (Grade 7)\">2005 CEMC Gauss (Grade 7)</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_7)_Problems\" title=\"2005 CEMC Gauss (Grade 7) Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_7)_Answer_Key\" title=\"2005 CEMC Gauss (Grade 7) Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://cemc.math.uwaterloo.ca/contests/past_contests.html\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_7)_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"2005 CEMC Gauss (Grade 7) Problems/Problem 7\">Problem 7</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_7)_Problems/Problem_9\" title=\"2005 CEMC Gauss (Grade 7) Problems/Problem 9\">Problem 9</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/i